{"step_index":392,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T22:03:33Z","input_tokens":2745,"cache_read_tokens":254608,"output_tokens":1807,"content":"# Resuming from a compaction\n\nYou are continuing work on the task described above, but you have lost access to the full conversation history, and need to resume work efficiently using the progress summary below:\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. Loaded active quiz from Firebase.\n\nrepalce it\nLoaded active quiz Locally.\n2. replace saving to firebase to just saving\nremove everytrace of firebase\n3. how do i add notes to code in html\n4. the indexhtml is still hardcoded with the quiz? i gave the index html to ai\n# gemini response\n\nHere are the answers to all 20 questions in the quiz, based on the `defaultQuiz` data embedded in the source code:\n\n1. **Which C statement selects one of many code blocks to run based on the value of an expression?**\n   * **Answer:** `switch`\n\n2. **Which type of expression can be used as the controlling expression of a switch in C?**\n   * **Answer:** `int or char`\n\n3. **Which keyword prevents execution from falling through to the next case?**\n   * **Answer:** `break`\n\n4. **When does the default label run?**\n   * **Answer:** When no case label matches\n\n5. **What is the output?**\n   ```c\n   int x = 2;\n   switch (x) {\n     case 1: printf(\"A\");\n     case 2: printf(\"B\");\n     case 3: printf(\"C\");\n   }\n   ```\n   * **Answer:** `BC`\n\n6. **What is the output?**\n   ```c\n   int x = 3;\n   switch (x) {\n     case 1: printf(\"1\"); break;\n     default: printf(\"D\");\n   }\n   ```\n   * **Answer:** `D`\n\n7. **Is the default label required in a switch statement?**\n   * **Answer:** No, it is optional\n\n8. **Which case label is valid in C?**\n   * **Answer:** `case 'A':`\n\n9. **What is the output?**\n   ```c\n   char c = 'b';\n   switch (c) {\n     case 'a': printf(\"1\"); break;\n     case 'b': printf(\"2\");\n     case 'c': printf(\"3\"); break;\n   }\n   ```\n   * **Answer:** `23`\n\n10. **What happens if two case labels in the same switch have the same constant value?**\n    * **Answer:** Compile-time error\n\n11. **Where can the default label be placed inside a switch?**\n    * **Answer:** Anywhere inside the switch\n\n12. **What is the output when x = 1?**\n    ```c\n    switch (x) {\n      case 1:\n      case 2: printf(\"Low\"); break;\n      case 3: printf(\"High\");\n    }\n    ```\n    * **Answer:** `Low`\n\n13. **Which is NOT allowed as the controlling expression of a switch in C?**\n    * **Answer:** A float variable, e.g. `switch(f)`\n\n14. **Which statement about case labels is true?**\n    * **Answer:** They must be constant expressions\n\n15. **What is the output?**\n    ```c\n    int x = 5;\n    switch (x % 2) {\n      case 0: printf(\"Even\"); break;\n      case 1: printf(\"Odd\"); break;\n    }\n    ```\n    * **Answer:** `Odd`\n\n16. **What is the output?**\n    ```c\n    int x = 1;\n    switch (x) {\n      default: printf(\"D\");\n      case 1: printf(\"1\"); break;\n      case 2: printf(\"2\");\n    }\n    ```\n    * **Answer:** `1`\n\n17. **When is switch preferred over an if-else if chain?**\n    * **Answer:** Comparing one variable against several constant values\n\n18. **What is the value printed?**\n    ```c\n    int a = 1;\n    switch (a) {\n      case 1: a++;\n      case 2: a += 2; break;\n      case 3: a = 10;\n    }\n    printf(\"%d\", a);\n    ```\n    * **Answer:** `4`\n\n19. **Which is the correct switch syntax?**\n    * **Answer:** `switch (x) { case 1: printf(\"One\"); break; }`\n\n20. **Can a switch statement be nested inside another switch statement in C?**\n    * **Answer:** Yes\n\n---\nPowered by [AI Exporter](https://saveai.net)\n5. proceed\n6. i updated fire store to\nrules_version = '2';\nservice cloud.firestore {\n  match /databases/{database}/documents {\n    match /quizzes/{quizId} {\n      allow read: if true;\n      allow write: if false;\n\n      match /submissions/{subId} {\n        allow create: if request.resource.data.keys().hasOnly(\n                           ['n','s','raw','sw','pen','sc','tot','ts','t','code','submittedAt'])\n                      && request.resource.data.n is string && request.resource.data.n.size() < 100\n                      && request.resource.data.s is string && request.resource.data.s.size() < 100;\n        allow read, update, delete: if false;\n      }\n    }\n    match /{document=**} {\n      allow read, write: if false;\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n\nmake sure our fiels is compatible to that\n7. proceed\n8. remove open student quiz button\n9. removebdownload quiz json button actually replace that with a  \nDownlaod QUIZ Json which will download index.html\nit should be downloadable even if i dont have index.html\nidk how you should do it tho maybe upload it to firebase?\nremove default quiz at firebaseconfig.js\n\ni updated firebase rule to\nrules_version = '2';\nservice cloud.firestore {\n  match /databases/{database}/documents {\n    match /quizzes/{quizId} {\n      allow read, write: if true;\n\n      match /submissions/{subId} {\n        allow create: if true;\n        allow read, update, delete: if false;\n      }\n    }\n    match /{document=**} {\n      allow read, write: if false;\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n\nmake sure our fiels our ocmpatible\n\n10. proceed\n\n<summary>\n1. **Task Overview**\n   - **Goal:** Transform a badly-built static quiz (`QUIZ06 (1) (1).html`) into a dual-site web app deployable to Vercel and backed by Firebase Firestore (project `sir-jasper-quiz`).\n   - **Student Quiz (`index.html`):** Renders quiz dynamically with live countdown timer, tab-switch violation penalty modal, auto-randomization of questions and choices, question-by-question feedback, base64 result code generation, and JSON result download. Crucially, **must contain zero hardcoded questions or answer keys** in static source code to prevent AI/view-source cheating.\n   - **Teacher Editor (`teacher.html`):** Auto-numbered question cards, tap-to-type question/distractor inputs, \"+\" button to append new questions, slide-out right-edge options drawer (`.edge-panel`) triggered by a side gear icon button, \"Save to Quiz\" button syncing directly to Firestore, and a `Download QUIZ Json` button that downloads `index.html`.\n   - **Target Firebase Config:**\n     - `apiKey`: `AIzaSyBkqJ9WvtXfGJt19XK7SLK9v5cJwp4EVII`\n     - `authDomain`: `sir-jasper-quiz.firebaseapp.com`\n     - `projectId`: `sir-jasper-quiz`\n   - **Active Firestore Rules:**\n     ```\n     rules_version = '2';\n     service cloud.firestore {\n       match /databases/{database}/documents {\n         match /quizzes/{quizId} {\n           allow read, write: if true;\n           match /submissions/{subId} {\n             allow create: if true;\n             allow read, update, delete: if false;\n           }\n         }\n         match /{document=**} { allow read, write: if false; }\n       }\n     }\n     ```\n\n2. **Progress**\n   - **Completed:**\n     - `firebase-config.js`: Cleaned to remove `defaultQuiz`. Now exports only initialized Firebase app, `db`, `getActiveQuiz`, `saveActiveQuiz`, and `saveSubmission`.\n     - `index.html`: Fully purged of `defaultQuiz`. Fetches dynamically from Firestore. Strict 11-key submission schema with `maxlength=\"99\"` on name/section. Rules match exact original phrasing with bold tags (`<b>20 seconds</b>` and `<b>-1 point</b>`). All traces of \"Firebase\" removed from visible UI.\n     - `quizzes/template` in Firestore: Seeded with the full `index.html` markup via REST API so it can be downloaded on any device without local files.\n     - `teacher.html`: Replaced button label with `Download QUIZ Json`. Removed `defaultQuiz` hardcoded data. Removed \"Open Student Quiz\" button. Removed \"Load Default C Quiz\" button. Removed intro paragraph. Side options gear icon and slide-out edge drawer fully functional.\n   - **In Progress / Just Interrupted:**\n     - Updating `teacher.html` lines 320–440:\n       1) In `loadTeacherQuiz()`, remove reference to `defaultQuiz` and initialize with `{ questions: [] }` if Firestore doc doesn't exist.\n       2) In `save-btn.onclick`, save to `quizzes/{quizId}` without old permission restrictions (now allowed with `allow read, write: if true`).\n       3) In `dl-quiz-btn.onclick`, implement downloading `index.html` (fetched from Firestore `quizzes/template`, fallback `fetch('index.html')`).\n     - Appending Non-Major Patch 1.0.9 to `HISTORY.md` per Rule 1.\n\n3. **Key Findings**\n   - Browser `file:///` protocol assigns origin `\"null\"`, which blocks ES module imports (`type=\"module\"` with relative paths). Using Google official compat scripts (`firebase-app-compat.js` and `firebase-firestore-compat.js`) allows native dual-mode execution for both double-clicking `.html` locally and hosting on Vercel.\n   - User explicitly requested: \"Downlaod QUIZ Json which will download index.html it should be downloadable even if i dont have index.html idk how you should do it tho maybe upload it to firebase?\". Solution: template stored in Firestore `quizzes/template`.\n\n4. **Errors & Fixes**\n   - **Error 1:** `Access to script at 'file://.../firebase-config.js' from origin 'null' has been blocked by CORS policy`\n     - *Cause:* Chrome/Edge blocks relative ES module imports from `file:///`.\n     - *Fix:* Replaced modular imports with Google Firebase CDN compat scripts loaded via standard `<script>` tags.\n   - **Error 2:** Gemini AI was able to extract all answers from `index.html`.\n     - *Cause:* `defaultQuiz` was embedded as a static fallback object in `index.html`.\n     - *Fix:* Completely purged `defaultQuiz` from `index.html`; questions are now loaded exclusively over the network at runtime.\n   - **Error 3:** 403 `PERMISSION_DENIED` on quiz write with previous rules (`allow write: if false`).\n     - *Cause:* User's previous Firestore rule write-locked `/quizzes/{quizId}`.\n     - *Fix:* User updated Firestore rules to `allow read, write: if true;` on `/quizzes/{quizId}` and `allow create: if true;` on `submissions`.\n\n5. **Active Context**\n   - Working Directory: `C:\\Users\\CxAdmin\\Desktop\\Exploit`\n   - Active files: `index.html`, `teacher.html`, `firebase-config.js`, `vercel.json`, `HISTORY.md`.\n   - Original file `QUIZ06 (1) (1).html` is UNTOUCHED per Rule 2 & 12.\n\n6. **Next Steps**\n   1. In `teacher.html`:\n      - Finish updating `loadTeacherQuiz()` to load from Firestore `quizzes/active` and fallback to empty `{ questions: [] }` (removing `defaultQuiz` reference).\n      - Wire `dl-quiz-btn.onclick` to fetch `index.html` from `db.collection(\"quizzes\").doc(\"template\").get()` (or fallback `fetch('index.html')`), and trigger a file download named `index.html` with type `text/html`.\n      - Wire `save-btn.onclick` to save to Firestore `quizzes/{quizId}`, update template in `quizzes/template`, and show `Saved Successfully to Student Quiz File! Quiz is live.`.\n   2. In `HISTORY.md`:\n      - Append Non-Major Patch 1.0.9 detailing:\n        - Removed `defaultQuiz` from `firebase-config.js` and `teacher.html`.\n        - Replaced JSON download button with `Download QUIZ Json` downloading `index.html`.\n        - Updated Firestore write integration for updated security rules.\n   3. Verification:\n      - Run `node scratch/verify_code.mjs` to ensure 0 comments/docstrings in `teacher.html`, `index.html`, `firebase-config.js`, `vercel.json`.\n      - Run headless Edge on `teacher.html` and `index.html` to confirm clean DOM rendering and zero errors.\n\n7. **Commitments & Constraints**\n   - **Rule 1 (`HISTORY.md`):** Every non-major patch must be appended below current entries with explanation of why. Do not revise or update existing entries.\n   - **Rule 2 & 12:** Prohibited from touching original files other than UI (`QUIZ06 (1) (1).html` must stay untouched). Do not build APK.\n   - **Rule 9:** **ZERO IN-CODE DOCUMENTATION:** No comments (`//`, `/*`, `<!--`), docstrings, or TODO/FIXME in any source code.\n   - **Rule 6 & 8:** Explicit user approval required for new plans before modifying code (plan was approved with \"proceed\" in this session).\n</summary>\n\nYou have the 1 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: implementation_plan]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/CxAdmin/.gemini/antigravity/brain/8f2bd4b5-d81b-4839-aa40-a5c3a5acaa6a/implementation_plan.md\nLast Edited: 2026-11-08T22:01:33Z\n\n# Conversation Logs\nStart with the compact transcript; if a step has `truncated_fields`, read only that specific line in `transcript_full.jsonl`:\n- `<appDataDir>/brain/<conversation-id>/.system_generated/logs/transcript.jsonl`\n- `<appDataDir>/brain/<conversation-id>/.system_generated/logs/transcript_full.jsonl`"}
