{"step_index":396,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T22:03:55Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-09T06:03:55+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-09T06:03:55+08:00\nShowing lines 1-47 of 47\n1: # Changelog\n2: \n3: ## [1.0.0] - 2026-11-09\n4: ### Major\n5: - Initial release of Firebase Firestore-backed Quiz Web Application for Vercel deployment.\n6: - Added student quiz interface (`index.html`) faithfully retaining original visual styling with anti-cheat detection, countdown timer, auto-randomization, base64 result code, and JSON file export.\n7: - Added teacher authoring portal (`teacher.html`) with auto-numbered dynamic question cards, question/distractor editing inputs, options modal for quiz behavior toggles, and direct Firestore synchronization.\n8: - Added modular Firebase configuration and Firestore data access layer (`firebase-config.js`).\n9: - Added static routing configuration for Vercel deployment (`vercel.json`).\n10: \n11: ### Non-Major (Patch 1.0.1)\n12: - Replaced relative ES module imports in `index.html` and `teacher.html` with Firebase compat scripts loaded via Google's official CDN.\n13: - Why: Browsers block relative ES module file imports under the `file:///` protocol due to origin `null` CORS restrictions when opening HTML files directly from local storage. The compat scripts enable native dual-mode execution for both local double-clicking and cloud hosting on Vercel.\n14: \n15: ### Non-Major (Patch 1.0.2)\n16: - Updated quiz start rules in `index.html` to exact original phrasing with bold tags: `Each question has <b>20 seconds</b>. When time runs out, it moves on automatically with no points.` and `Every alt-tab or switch to another tab/app costs <b>-1 point</b>.`\n17: - Why: User requested direct copy of exact instruction text with bold emphasis on 20 seconds and violation deduction.\n18: \n19: ### Non-Major (Patch 1.0.3)\n20: - Transformed options UI in `teacher.html` into a slide-over edge panel triggered by a docked side icon button.\n21: - Renamed save button to 'Save to Quiz' and updated success alert text to 'Saved Successfully to Student Quiz File! Quiz is live.'.\n22: - Removed 'Load Default C Quiz' button and the instructional introductory paragraph.\n23: - Why: User requested side edge panel navigation, custom button text, and cleaner interface.\n24: \n25: ### Non-Major (Patch 1.0.4)\n26: - Updated status message in `teacher.html` from 'Loaded active quiz from Firebase.' to 'Loaded active quiz Locally.'.\n27: - Why: User requested wording adjustment for local quiz load indication.\n28: \n29: ### Non-Major (Patch 1.0.5)\n30: - Replaced 'Saving to Firebase...' with 'Saving...' in `teacher.html`.\n31: - Removed UI-visible references to Firebase in `index.html` and `teacher.html` (e.g. initial connection prompt updated to 'Loading...', error messages generalized to 'Database is not initialized.').\n32: - Why: User requested removal of all Firebase naming traces from user-facing text and status prompts.\n33: \n34: ### Non-Major (Patch 1.0.6)\n35: - Completely removed `defaultQuiz` and all hardcoded question and answer key arrays from `index.html`.\n36: - Updated `loadQuiz()` to exclusively query and retrieve questions from the remote database at runtime.\n37: - Why: Prevented answer key leakage and AI extraction from source code inspection.\n38: \n39: ### Non-Major (Patch 1.0.7)\n40: - Aligned student submission payload in `index.html` with updated Firestore security rules (enforced strictly 11 allowed keys `['n','s','raw','sw','pen','sc','tot','ts','t','code','submittedAt']` and `maxlength=\"99\"` on name/section).\n41: - Added 'Download Quiz JSON' backup button and security-rule error feedback in `teacher.html`.\n42: - Why: Complied with updated Firestore security rules (`allow write: if false` on quizzes and strict submission schema).\n43: \n44: ### Non-Major (Patch 1.0.8)\n45: - Removed 'Open Student Quiz' navigation button from the top header card in `teacher.html`.\n46: - Why: User requested removal of the student portal shortcut link.\n47: "}
