{"step_index":398,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-08T22:03:59Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-09T06:03:59+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-09T06:03:59+08:00\nShowing lines 1-55 of 55\n1: # Implementation Plan: Download Student Quiz HTML, Remove defaultQuiz, & Align with Updated Rules\n2: \n3: ## 1. Overview of Requested Changes\n4: 1. **Remove `defaultQuiz` from [firebase-config.js](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/firebase-config.js)**:\n5:    - Purge the static `defaultQuiz` definition and 20 hardcoded switch-case questions from `firebase-config.js`.\n6: 2. **Download Student Quiz (`index.html`) from [teacher.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/teacher.html)**:\n7:    - Replace the previous JSON export button with a **`Download QUIZ Json`** button.\n8:    - When clicked, this button generates and downloads the complete standalone student quiz file (`index.html`).\n9:    - To ensure `index.html` is downloadable on any machine even if the local file is not present:\n10:      - On save or on demand, the student quiz template is synchronized with Firestore (`quizzes/template`).\n11:      - The download handler retrieves the content from Firestore (or fallback `fetch('index.html')` / embedded template) and triggers a browser download named `index.html`.\n12: 3. **Firestore Security Rules Alignment**:\n13:    - The user updated Firestore rules to allow read and write on `quizzes/{quizId}`:\n14:      ```\n15:      match /quizzes/{quizId} {\n16:        allow read, write: if true;\n17:        match /submissions/{subId} {\n18:          allow create: if true;\n19:          allow read, update, delete: if false;\n20:        }\n21:      }\n22:      ```\n23:    - Update `teacher.html` save handler so writes proceed cleanly without old permission restriction workarounds.\n24: \n25: ---\n26: \n27: ## 2. File Modifications\n28: \n29: ### 2.1 [firebase-config.js](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/firebase-config.js)\n30: - Delete `export const defaultQuiz = { ... };`.\n31: - Update `getActiveQuiz` to return `null` if the document is not found.\n32: \n33: ### 2.2 [teacher.html](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/teacher.html)\n34: - Change button markup to:\n35:   `<button id=\"dl-quiz-btn\" class=\"sec\" type=\"button\">Download QUIZ Json</button>`\n36: - In `save-btn` click handler:\n37:   - Save quiz settings and questions to `quizzes/{quizId}` in Firestore (now fully allowed under the updated rules).\n38:   - Also store the student quiz HTML template in `quizzes/template` so it is permanently accessible across devices.\n39: - In `dl-quiz-btn` click handler:\n40:   - Retrieve the student quiz HTML (from Firestore `quizzes/template`, fallback `fetch('index.html')`, or offline template).\n41:   - Create a blob (`text/html`) and initiate a file download named `index.html`.\n42: \n43: ### 2.3 [HISTORY.md](file:///c:/Users/CxAdmin/Desktop/Exploit/HISTORY.md)\n44: - Append Non-Major Patch 1.0.9 documenting the removal of `defaultQuiz` from `firebase-config.js` and the implementation of the `Download QUIZ Json` button downloading `index.html`.\n45: \n46: ---\n47: \n48: ## 3. Verification Plan (Rules 3 & 10)\n49: 1. **Source Code Audit**:\n50:    - Confirm `firebase-config.js` contains 0 occurrences of `defaultQuiz` or hardcoded question text.\n51:    - Confirm `teacher.html` has zero in-code comments per Rule 9.\n52: 2. **Download Functionality Verification**:\n53:    - Test `dl-quiz-btn` in `teacher.html`: verify it downloads `index.html` with valid HTML structure.\n54: 3. **Firestore Live Write Verification**:\n55:    - Test saving a quiz from `teacher.html` against live Firestore `sir-jasper-quiz` to verify HTTP 200 success under the new `allow read, write: if true;` rule."}
